# Work Closeout Constraints

- **Local-Only Execution:** Closeout content must stay on this Mac. Reject network AI providers (`provider` must be `disabled`). Do not add telemetry, analytics, or cloud closeout adapters. A private Git remote for source backup is allowed; never push secrets, live `work-closeout.json`, or evidence sessions.
- **Credential Protection:** Never place credentials, API keys, or secrets in `work-closeout.json`.
- **Read-Only Discovery:** When interacting with Obsidian, read only a bounded prefix of each note (frontmatter and title). Refuse to create, rename, or overwrite existing vaults or project notes.
- **Artifact Isolation:** The configured `artifactDirectory` must live entirely outside every directory listed in `allowedRoots` to prevent the closeout from collecting its own drafts and logs.
- **Command Sanitization:** Reject shell composition, network, privilege escalation, destructive, or app-launch commands within `verificationCommands`.
- **Non-Destructive Writes:** File writes must be atomic, session-specific, and never overwrite existing files. An explicit approval control is mandatory before writing to any Obsidian or report directory.
- **Strict Provenance:** Deterministic drafts must remain conservative and state only what the included local sources explicitly support, without fabricating context.
